{
  "schema": 2,
  "app": "clinic_photos",
  "module": "clinic_photos.tests.test_file_policy",
  "case_class": "ProtectedFileBoundaryTests",
  "isolation": "One case per isolated native execution. A protected denial latches this app's abort for the whole execution, so cases must never share an execution and the production latch is never cleared.",
  "selection_contract": "bench --site <site> run-tests --app <app> --module <case module> --case <case class> --test <bare_method>. Each case may declare its own module/case_class; cases that declare neither inherit the manifest-level pair (schema-1 compatibility). A case with readiness 'blocked' is never selectable and no command is generated for it.",
  "acceptance": "Every executable manifest case must report exactly one passing result, in its own native execution, with provenance emitted by the selected test itself (identity + per-invocation nonce) and with a versioned, observed disposal confirmation covering the run (run id, site, project, source and contract digests, per-case nonces and raw-output hashes) and the residue it created (rows AND protected storage keys). Skips, missing/duplicate/extra results, identity or nonce mismatch, failures and an unobserved disposal are acceptance failures. A failing case still surrenders its residue. Empty residue is not proof of filesystem cleanliness. Blocked cases are excluded from the matrix, never selected, and never counted as a pass. 'expects_denial'/'latches_abort' describe the in-process owner/latch protocol only; the publication child refusals asserted by pub.process.* cases are process outcome assertions, not owner-latch denials.",
